WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.830
STEPHANIE WONG: Hi.

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:01.490
I'm Stephanie.

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:03.830
And today I'll be showcasing
the digital shopping

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:05.510
journey of a beauty
consumer and how

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:08.840
retailers can improve customer
experience and engagement.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.630
With the COVID-19 outbreak
and resulting disruptions,

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:14.630
consumers were left homebound
for days at a stretch.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:16.880
A recent Google survey
shows beauty consumers

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.830
initially purchased
less products,

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.110
but recently have
a revived interest

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:25.550
in beauty categories like
makeup, sunscreen, and shampoo.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:29.090
They've also shifted heavily
towards online purchasing.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:31.520
Of course, with online
shopping, consumers

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.070
are experiencing the same
pain points that have always

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.570
come with beauty shopping.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.220
It's hard to choose
the right product,

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:38.840
envision the product
on themselves,

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.780
and decide on a product
without prior brand experience.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.480
Today I'll show you how you
can empower your customers

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.700
with a seamless online
shopping experience

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.560
and carry them from
product discovery

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.230
to consideration to purchase.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:52.190
Meet Mary.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:54.643
Mary is a marketing
consultant by day.

00:00:54.643 --> 00:00:56.060
Even though her
city does not have

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.770
a shelter-at-home
order in place,

00:00:57.770 --> 00:00:59.510
Mary is working from home.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:00.620
But summer is here.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.540
And Mary has a
socially distant picnic

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.340
planned for this weekend with
some of her close friends.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.880
It's outdoors and
feels relatively safe.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.120
She plans to wear a mask on
her way to and from the park.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.130
But she also wants to
look great on her rare day

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:16.040
out Mary decides to experiment
with a dramatic look

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.510
for her eyes.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.720
To start, Mary searches
YouTube for a daytime eye look

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.850
and finds a full tutorial on it.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:25.350
She loves this look on
the influencer, of course.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.500
But she's not sure
it will work on her.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.760
Luckily, she notices a Try
It On button under the video.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:33.800
She's able to try on
the look on her eyes

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.960
and even experiment with
different colors using

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.720
a built-in augmented
reality feature.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.300
Looks like the blue
really pops on her.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.360
All of this works using
machine learning and ARCore.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.240
The technology dynamically
detects the user's face shape

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.310
and attributes rather
than static images.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.120
This allows you to create
rich, engaging experiences

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:54.620
for your customers.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:57.350
And with an integrated shopping
button, users like Mary

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.750
can quickly land on
the Shopping page.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:02.270
To check if the eyeshadow
will suit her skin tone,

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:04.790
Mary can simply head to her
integrated digital shopping

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:08.210
assistant and ask that
question using voice.

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:10.340
The assistant can
also show her reviews

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:12.170
and answer any common queries.

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:13.880
With a digital
shopping assistant,

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:15.860
you can introduce
new interactive ways

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:18.120
for your customers to
experience your brand.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.960
Dialogflow is the underlying
technology for the shopping

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.790
assistant and can
be used to easily

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:26.420
train a chat bot on your product
graph for a specific SKU,

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.540
from product details, or
frequently asked questions.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:31.400
Mary adds this item to her cart.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.950
And as she does that, Mary
receives recommendations

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.440
on additional products to buy.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:39.830
Retailers today are increasingly
centralizing their user data

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:42.590
in Google's BigQuery
data analytics platform

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:44.510
and then building
personalization

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.600
and recommendation models
on top of this data.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.210
Here we're able to take a
look at her previous purchase

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:52.550
history, as well as
the items in her cart,

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:54.860
to provide more relevant
recommendations to complete

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:56.360
her purchase.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.850
As Mary scrolls through the
frequently bought together

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:01.040
and other items of
interest, she remembers

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:03.170
she could replace her cleanser.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:07.700
She searches for dry skin
cleanser and adds to her cart.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.800
Additionally, she remembers
she is running out

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.360
of her favorite sunscreen.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:13.880
So she clicks on Vision
Search and simply snaps

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.380
a picture of the
sunscreen container

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.060
that's right next to her desk.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.520
She uses it to search for
the product on the retailer

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:21.950
website, and it
matches with a click.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:25.070
Today's retail search is
keyword-centric, driven largely

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:28.310
by manual merchandising rules,
matching tokens or words

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.560
in the query to
data in the catalog,

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.580
and use of limited data
from retailers' logs.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.100
Google Cloud Search for
Retail provides retailers

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:40.220
with high-quality product search
results for their websites

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.930
and mobile applications.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:46.070
Users can begin a query via
voice, image, text, and barcode

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:48.650
and get to their choice
of products faster.

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:50.870
With everything she
wanted to buy and more,

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:53.150
Mary finalizes a time
that works for her

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:55.460
for curbside pickup
at her nearest store

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.720
and wraps up by
paying with GPay.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:01.640
Contactless feels good not
just in store, but online, too.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.250
Now all she needs to do
is go pick up her order.

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.470
Thankfully, the store
was just a mile away.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.240
With integrated
maps, she can easily

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:10.790
find her way for her
scheduled curbside pickup

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:12.710
right from her
confirmation mail,

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:15.320
beauty shopping
made fun and easy.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:17.420
Most of Mary's journey
is on the site,

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.250
so why have a
disconnected experience

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.720
before reaching the site?

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:24.200
Mary's journey demonstrates how
Google Cloud's AI/ML-powered

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:27.200
products and solutions can
create a more seamless user

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.780
journey and captivate
customers with engaging

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:31.970
and hyperpersonalized moments.

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:34.460
What are you solving for?

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:37.010
To learn more about Google
Cloud's Retail solutions,

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.330
check out the link here.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:41.380
[MUSIC FADING OUT]

